 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Chester the beaver put the doorknob by the hinge. Nobody got in.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.327
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Trust the teeth!\" he said. So why are doorknobs always far from the hinges?",
   "s": 3.527,
   "e": 6.858
  },
  {
   "text": "Mrs. Plum pushed the library door for ten minutes. It moved one inch.",
   "s": 7.158,
   "e": 10.684
  },
  {
   "text": "Big Lars, the strongest man in Pinecone Hollow, pushed until his hat popped off. Two inches.",
   "s": 10.884,
   "e": 15.68
  },
  {
   "text": "So Chester added a second knob, right next to the first. \"Trust the teeth!\"",
   "s": 15.88,
   "e": 19.684
  },
  {
   "text": "By Friday, forty people were stuck outside, reading through the window.",
   "s": 19.804,
   "e": 23.078
  },
  {
   "text": "So Chester hired Gertrude the elephant. She pushed. The door opened. So did the wall.",
   "s": 23.278,
   "e": 26.841
  },
  {
   "text": "So why is the far edge so easy?",
   "s": 27.041,
   "e": 28.43
  },
  {
   "text": "A door spins around its hinges, so the far edge works like a long lever.",
   "s": 28.73,
   "e": 32.348
  },
  {
   "text": "Push far from the hinge, and one finger does it. Push next to it, and you need an elephant.",
   "s": 32.748,
   "e": 36.87
  },
  {
   "text": "Chester moved every knob to the edge. Mrs. Plum opened the door with her pinky.",
   "s": 37.07,
   "e": 41.328
  },
  {
   "text": "Gertrude still works there. She holds the door.",
   "s": 41.528,
   "e": 43.624
  }
 ],
